Author: Frank Stettner <frank-stettner@gmx.net>
Date:   Thu Jul 23 11:15:12 2026 +0200

    libusb1: update 1.0.27 -> 1.0.30
    
    Bump libusb1 to pick up features libsigrok needs on Windows, so the
    libusb "special branch" and the RAW_IO patch can be droped.
    
    - Windows event abstraction: libsigrok used to require a custom libusb
      branch (github.com/uwehermann/libusb) because libusb emulated Unix
      file descriptors/poll() on top of native Windows HANDLEs, which didn't
      work reliably for libsigrok's async USB I/O. This was replaced
      upstream with a native per-platform events abstraction (pipe/poll on
      POSIX, `WaitForMultipleObjects()` on Windows), merged with commit
      libusb/libusb@d67eb5beaa44, PR libusb/libusb#252.
    
    - WinUSB RAW_IO: The sigrok MXE build previously carried a local patch
      that set the WinUSB RAW_IO pipe policy unconditionally for every
      endpoint. Upstream has now reintroduced RAW_IO support for the WinUSB
      backend, but as an explicit, opt-in, per-endpoint API
      (`LIBUSB_OPTION_WINUSB_RAW_IO` via `libusb_set_option()`) rather than
      an unconditional policy. Merged via libusb/libusb#1069,
      libusb/libusb#1208 and finally libusb/libusb#1512, commit
      libusb/libusb@3dac3f2, included in release 1.0.30.

